Subject:  Why PC-LISP doesn't work


It looks like a lot of people don't know about the 64K limit on notes files.
A single notes entry can't contain more than 64K characters.  Even splitting
PC-LISP in half doesn't bring the pieces under the limit.  So if all of you
out there would break your huge files into hunks smaller than 64K, that would
solve a lot of problems with downloading source and object files.

